      "a": "${{\\text{CaS}}{{\\text{O}}_{4(s)}} \\leftrightarrow {\\text{C}}{{\\text{a}}^{2 + }}_{(aq)} + SO_{4(aq)}^{2 - }} $\n${{K_{sp}} = \\left[ {{\\text{C}}{{\\text{a}}^{2 + }}} \\right]\\left[ {{\\text{SO}}_4^{2 - }} \\right]} $\nLet the solubility of ${\\text{CaS}}{{\\text{O}}_4}$ be ${\\text{s}}$.\nThen, ${K_{sp}} = {s^2}$\n${9.1 \\times {{10}^{ - 6}} = {s^2}} $\n${s = 3.02 \\times {{10}^{ - 3}}\\;{\\text{mol}}/{\\text{L}}} $\nMolecular mass of ${\\text{CaS}}{{\\text{O}}_4} = 136\\;{\\text{g}}/{\\text{mol}}$\nSolubility of ${\\text{CaS}}{{\\text{O}}_4}$ in gram/L\n${ = 3.02 \\times {{10}^{ - 3}} \\times 136} $\n${ = 0.41\\;{\\text{g}}/{\\text{L}}} $\nThis means that we need $1\\;{\\text{L}}$ of water to dissolve $0.41\\;{\\text{g}}$ of ${\\text{CaS}}{{\\text{O}}_4}$\nTherefore, to dissolve $1\\;{\\text{g}}$ of ${\\text{CaS}}{{\\text{O}}_4}$ we require $ = \\dfrac{1}{{0.41}}\\;{\\text{L}} = 2.44\\;{\\text{L}}$ of water."
